,"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLMetronome","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Note","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Note","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome-note type defines the appearance of a note within a metric relationship mark."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note","title":"MXLMetronome.Note"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNoteKindValue":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNoteKindValue","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLNoteKindValue","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNoteKindValue","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The note-type-value type is used for the MusicXML type element and represents the graphic note type, from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1024th (shortest) to maxima (longest)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNoteKindValue","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotekindvalue","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note/kind":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNoteKindValueO","text":"MXLNoteKindValue"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The metronome-type element works like the type element in defining metric relationships.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/kind","title":"kind","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/kind"}}}